From 65ea19cac00cef8a942e8566c5e88b8e632045f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ilyatbn <ilyatbn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:42:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: emulate the geometry stage - GS as a compute
 shader, three-pass draw (exynos-woa G25 0125)

Panfrost has no geometry stage. CreateGeometryShader translates the DXBC GS into a compute shader (ShaderTGSI.c
gs_as_cs: inputs preloaded from the VS outputs, EMIT/CUT -> stores of fixed vertex slots + a restart index buffer).
A draw with it bound (GsEmu.cpp): VS stream-output variant + rasterizer discard -> A; GS compute -> B, I; I drawn as
an indexed strip with primitive restart through a passthrough VS; application state restored (GS/CS constant buffers
and the rasterizer are tracked now). D3D10UMD_GS_DUMP=1 logs A/B/I: diagnosis only. d3dgs 3/3 pixel-exact vs WARP.
---
